The bar is a full-width element that is scaled with `transform`. The shine is a one-time keyframe animation:

```html
<div class="shipping-progress" role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="0">
  <p class="shipping-progress__text">Add €50.00 more for free shipping</p>
  <div class="shipping-progress__track">
    <div class="shipping-progress__bar"></div>
  </div>
</div>
```

```css
.shipping-progress { margin: 1rem 0; }

.shipping-progress__text { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }

.shipping-progress__track {
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  background: #e5e7eb;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.shipping-progress__bar {
  position: relative;
  height: 100%;
  background: #16a34a;
  transform-origin: left center;
  transform: scaleX(calc(var(--progress, 0) / 100));
  transition: transform 0.4s ease-out;
}

/* One-time shine when the goal is reached */
.shipping-progress__bar::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6), transparent);
  transform: translateX(-100%);
  opacity: 0;
}

.shipping-progress.is-complete .shipping-progress__bar::after {
  animation: shine 0.8s ease-out 0.4s 1 forwards;
}

@keyframes shine {
  0%   { transform: translateX(-100%); opacity: 1; }
  100% { transform: translateX(100%);  opacity: 0; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .shipping-progress__bar { transition: none; }
  .shipping-progress.is-complete .shipping-progress__bar::after { animation: none; }
}
```

Small JS to drive it:

```javascript
const box = document.querySelector(".shipping-progress");

function updateShipping(cartTotal, threshold = 50) {
  const percent = Math.min(100, Math.round((cartTotal / threshold) * 100));
  box.style.setProperty("--progress", percent);
  box.setAttribute("aria-valuenow", percent);
  box.classList.toggle("is-complete", percent === 100);
  box.querySelector(".shipping-progress__text").textContent =
    percent === 100
      ? "Free shipping!"
      : `Add €${(threshold - cartTotal).toFixed(2)} more for free shipping`;
}
```

**Green Notes**
- **CSS transition and keyframes instead of a JS animation loop** (reduces client E): the browser runs the animation itself, and your JS only sets one variable when the cart changes. In Green Metrics Tool browser benchmarks, a 20-second CSS `@keyframes` animation used about 10% less CPU energy than a `requestAnimationFrame` version.
- **`transform: scaleX()` instead of animating `width`:** it avoids layout work on every frame, and the compositor can handle it.
- **The shine runs once** (`1 forwards`), not `infinite`. A looping animation would keep the page busy for as long as the cart stays open.
- `prefers-reduced-motion` turns the motion off for users who ask for it.

